#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188034 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188327 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c80ef8f-1073-5e41-bec3-860209a731bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional Mass Function"}] :question/id #uuid "6cdc2b0e-a968-5d95-8fb6-5d469a5920b9" :question/math-academy-id "e-10302" :question/problem "| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f_{Y|X}(y \\,|\\, 3)$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\textrm{Var}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=3\\big]$ given that the conditional probability mass function $f_{Y|X}(y \\,|\\, 3)$ is shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is $\\mu_{Y|3} = \\dfrac{8}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=3] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)]-{\\mu }_{Y|3}^{2} \\\\  & =[(1)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}+(2)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}+(4)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}]-{(\\frac{8}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}+8-\\frac{64}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{17}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188035 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188328 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92a52324-627c-5796-bc4f-ddeb5380f129" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Using Column Totals"}] :question/id #uuid "49a039ae-dbe1-5faa-a9a7-014bd9549c03" :question/math-academy-id "e-10306" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{16}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{16}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\textrm{Var}\\big[X \\,|\\, Y=2\\big]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is $\\mu_{X|2}=\\dfrac{10}{9}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find $f_{X | Y}(x \\,|\\, y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution of $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{16}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{16}$ |\n| $f_Y(y)$ | $\\dfrac{9}{16}$ | $\\dfrac{7}{16}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\nf_{X | Y}(x \\,|\\, y)  = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_Y(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y{:}$\n\n| $f_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{8}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{4}{7}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{9}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{7}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=2] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)]-{\\mu }_{X|2}^{2} \\\\  & =[{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{8}{9}+{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}]-{(\\frac{10}{9})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{9}+\\frac{4}{9}-\\frac{100}{81} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{81}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188046 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abfaf356-6b74-5dfd-8070-e3a60dc372c5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Using Row Totals"}] :question/id #uuid "3764cb54-7fd2-584a-9dc7-eda88368b032" :question/math-academy-id "e-10352" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{3}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\textrm{Var}\\big[Y \\,|\\, X=1\\big]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is $\\mu_{Y|1} = \\dfrac{9}{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find $f_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ | $f_X(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{2}{5}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{3}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{5}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{10}$ | $\\dfrac{3}{5}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\nf_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x)  = \\dfrac{f(x,y)}{f_X(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x{:}$\n\n| $f_{Y | X}(y \\,|\\, x)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{4}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ | $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)]-{\\mu }_{Y|1}^{2} \\\\  & =[{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+{3}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}]-{(\\frac{9}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}+1+\\frac{9}{2}-\\frac{81}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188635 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188327 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c80ef8f-1073-5e41-bec3-860209a731bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional Mass Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8efe7779-a68e-5320-9296-47bd49330142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.69" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186091} {:answer/id #uuid "b9f78844-51fc-53d4-8e04-b0c325e2012f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186092} {:answer/id #uuid "0a1760c4-2536-5c77-a1ab-0e41464ef0b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186093} {:answer/id #uuid "0b97bdb2-55bb-51a0-a1e5-c0f1c24cfb35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186094} {:answer/id #uuid "53d94e20-9ee4-5882-97b4-bfc5c3196345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186095}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53d94e20-9ee4-5882-97b4-bfc5c3196345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.44" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186095} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8b5e94e-afe5-5762-95d7-8bafbffc617d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186090}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88a6f652-2dd2-5b0b-9432-59ef465ca5aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-145561" :question/problem "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ | $0.5$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)$ is shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|1}=1.4.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)]-{\\mu }_{Y|1}^{2} \\\\  & =[(0)^{2}\\cdot 0.1+(1)^{2}\\cdot 0.4+(2)^{2}\\cdot 0.5]-(1.4)^{2} \\\\  & =0+0.4+2-1.96 \\\\  & =0.44.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188637 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188328 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92a52324-627c-5796-bc4f-ddeb5380f129" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Using Column Totals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2452ce83-dc52-55f6-8ada-4270840e5f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186103} {:answer/id #uuid "3112bbd0-2efd-5af4-9183-d529b43787f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186104} {:answer/id #uuid "32a79aa0-324a-576c-b24a-9dda030a3055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186105} {:answer/id #uuid "496b21b0-10f4-5ed9-a567-35580e353507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186106} {:answer/id #uuid "7c5cc2f6-63db-5ee3-a19a-a655c587bd7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "496b21b0-10f4-5ed9-a567-35580e353507" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186106} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b0e8466-e71c-51fa-a1f3-58418768c396" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186102}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "87429b89-e333-5492-85d9-bf5d6ddc4038" :question/math-academy-id "q-145581" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=0]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|0}=\\frac{1}{3}.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution of $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=0] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)]-{\\mu }_{X|0}^{2} \\\\  & =[(0)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}+(1)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}]-(\\frac{1}{3})^{2} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188680 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abfaf356-6b74-5dfd-8070-e3a60dc372c5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Using Row Totals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b20165e2-6fe7-54aa-8006-6fcf097ac4fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186361} {:answer/id #uuid "d91ffcfa-8adc-595a-b349-50d0122ff2db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186362} {:answer/id #uuid "f9187b5e-22bc-5d31-abd4-265dd8a9df03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186363} {:answer/id #uuid "2b8a778f-9674-5eb0-98b5-530ecc1f069f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186364} {:answer/id #uuid "34075399-76f6-5159-a3eb-3e2a37a1ff99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9187b5e-22bc-5d31-abd4-265dd8a9df03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186363} :answer-field/id #uuid "6762d125-e9d7-5f02-9226-4a00e4721756" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "60cb8cd8-f4a1-51b2-afe3-57e452f5f729" :question/math-academy-id "q-146159" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=0]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|0}=1.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=0] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|0}^{2} \\\\  & =[{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}]-{(1)}^{2} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{2}+1-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527927 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188327 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c80ef8f-1073-5e41-bec3-860209a731bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional Mass Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19a8bec2-48ba-5a11-a243-ad1cfdb0c57b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527363} {:answer/id #uuid "7fc5004c-bab4-52e2-ace0-ae6162e110d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527554} {:answer/id #uuid "b8227aeb-2f23-5441-8fc0-8c3dbb03d4b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527687} {:answer/id #uuid "de737258-a686-5bef-bdde-8f04025a1062" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527749} {:answer/id #uuid "fcad7b2f-d2c4-56a4-a9ff-d30db2074f4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527796}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcad7b2f-d2c4-56a4-a9ff-d30db2074f4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527796} :answer-field/id #uuid "c53ed922-aca5-5bca-99bf-697d183ea725" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "315997a1-7d2c-5dee-aeca-23b06ca1daaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-146201" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}, & x=5 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}, & x=10 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=2]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ is shown above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|2}=8.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)]-{\\mu }_{X|2}^{2} \\\\  & =[(5)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}+(10)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{5}]-(8)^{2} \\\\  & =10+60-64 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188327 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c80ef8f-1073-5e41-bec3-860209a731bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional Mass Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "310fc6a4-db62-5f96-8df4-bbd6b181d385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527410} {:answer/id #uuid "87176957-585a-58b1-ba8a-7520d939ae2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527571} {:answer/id #uuid "b8cfef22-7523-58f7-9f2e-991730673fa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527688} {:answer/id #uuid "cceac401-e703-5120-be30-1c346fcae5ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527722} {:answer/id #uuid "f53eb1ee-a782-5e0d-ad7e-d9c94d71e493" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527785}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f53eb1ee-a782-5e0d-ad7e-d9c94d71e493" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527785} :answer-field/id #uuid "079de692-aa36-527f-b17f-d2c9a0e53c01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f6a4dc1-cc0e-50e8-a876-123c929a6728" :question/math-academy-id "q-146202" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.4, & x=1 \\\\ 0.6, & x=2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=1]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)$ is shown above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|1}=1.6.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)]-{\\mu }_{X|1}^{2} \\\\  & =[(1)^{2}\\cdot 0.4+(2)^{2}\\cdot 0.6]-(1.6)^{2} \\\\  & =0.4+2.4-2.56 \\\\  & =0.24.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527966 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188327 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c80ef8f-1073-5e41-bec3-860209a731bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional Mass Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39c73cfa-7b32-590c-b75b-0204826dff2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527422} {:answer/id #uuid "39dd785e-5174-5e6e-b059-c2712b64a71e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527423} {:answer/id #uuid "54955e88-70a2-5393-9107-0e28fe8834fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527466} {:answer/id #uuid "6fbf2e95-fb3f-53c7-ad6e-69eb5f31932a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527515} {:answer/id #uuid "ba2deb2d-5233-59f1-9ed9-14564cf52445" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527691}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fbf2e95-fb3f-53c7-ad6e-69eb5f31932a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527515} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a9293fa-0ff1-56b4-a14c-8acca9e82920" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "86c9830c-c21b-52dd-a632-55f72d300bd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-146204" :question/problem "| $x$ | $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{5}{8}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ is shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|4}=3.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)]-{\\mu }_{X|4}^{2} \\\\  & =[(0)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}+(2)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+(4)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{8}]-(3)^{2} \\\\  & =0+1+10-9 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527950 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188327 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c80ef8f-1073-5e41-bec3-860209a731bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional Mass Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dd6de30-6014-5a8c-958c-74bee530a51f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.08" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527336} {:answer/id #uuid "10a9c696-6e92-5cef-a6d2-a7fbbfa35df6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.75" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527343} {:answer/id #uuid "67f5954e-0888-5e41-aa25-993cc635c802" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527504} {:answer/id #uuid "ccb54557-388a-55ab-b4f8-52bc95263e1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.99" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527721} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb2a9d4-480e-5425-b3fa-01ec4e2f3b34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527725}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccb54557-388a-55ab-b4f8-52bc95263e1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.99" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527721} :answer-field/id #uuid "4eca249b-fcf1-5eef-8bb3-bbd4ab981b54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527835}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "611fada0-4ebb-55c6-bcaf-8dccb0c75bca" :question/math-academy-id "q-146208" :question/problem "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,8)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.45, & y=4 \\\\ 0.55, & y=6 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=8]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,8)$ is shown above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|8}=5.1.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=8] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,8)]-{\\mu }_{Y|8}^{2} \\\\  & =[(4)^{2}\\cdot 0.45+(6)^{2}\\cdot 0.55]-(5.1)^{2} \\\\  & =7.2+19.8-26.01 \\\\  & =0.99.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abfaf356-6b74-5dfd-8070-e3a60dc372c5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Using Row Totals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cf8e160-2051-5377-beb9-7f358fa12cec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527334} {:answer/id #uuid "ca613bca-62eb-519c-a990-d494e25f04b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527714} {:answer/id #uuid "cfd80d10-6b1c-5684-a3dc-37d716ebf7e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527727} {:answer/id #uuid "fc8fe0a7-5a62-53ed-9ad4-a69d4dc8c276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527795} {:answer/id #uuid "fd2d7ec6-a6e6-5a31-bdbf-78782edf7758" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca613bca-62eb-519c-a990-d494e25f04b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527714} :answer-field/id #uuid "c14a0fdb-ff7e-57f0-b03c-3708c9d22c3b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3104fe5f-1fab-5144-bd0b-8c85fa4d01fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-146225" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{5}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=2]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|2}=\\frac{11}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{5}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{5}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=2] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2)]-{\\mu }_{Y|2}^{2} \\\\  & =[{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+{4}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+{8}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}]-{(\\frac{11}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =1+4+32-\\frac{121}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511574 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abfaf356-6b74-5dfd-8070-e3a60dc372c5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Using Row Totals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46451ad3-292e-5818-b57f-512919c1b762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510940} {:answer/id #uuid "85f1ae38-1f12-5af1-9e47-1e397e55e732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511058} {:answer/id #uuid "9848b01d-ae3d-5b11-a03c-4137d1ec2d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511099} {:answer/id #uuid "e44fbbd6-2948-5df7-8863-f9b14dba4caa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511260} {:answer/id #uuid "f1966108-9bd3-50ba-ae71-0b6fda1b9652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e44fbbd6-2948-5df7-8863-f9b14dba4caa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511260} :answer-field/id #uuid "273fb450-78e1-578c-ad1c-ea60b9f9611a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e9ff9199-1184-598e-a945-b789f3d5b0b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-146236" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=5$ | $Y=10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{4}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{25}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{25}$ | $\\frac{1}{25}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=6]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|6}=\\frac{15}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=5$ | $Y=10$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{4}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{25}$ | $\\frac{23}{25}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{25}$ | $\\frac{1}{25}$ | $\\frac{2}{25}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=5$ | $Y=10$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{20}{23}$ | $\\frac{3}{23}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=6] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,6)]-{\\mu }_{Y|6}^{2} \\\\  & =[{5}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+{10}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}]-{(\\frac{15}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{2}+50-\\frac{225}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527932 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abfaf356-6b74-5dfd-8070-e3a60dc372c5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Using Row Totals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e20a1e7-c143-53bc-878e-ea30164f1481" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527337} {:answer/id #uuid "634b9a3d-06ab-59c4-8af6-665347876113" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527495} {:answer/id #uuid "68106bf3-93d0-57f1-baec-9d90f724b12b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527505} {:answer/id #uuid "95fc6287-af80-5279-939b-bc5232fd84f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527606} {:answer/id #uuid "c6e1a5fe-ed76-5dc0-83b1-3c95dde85b9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6e1a5fe-ed76-5dc0-83b1-3c95dde85b9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527707} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0780126-c4c2-5d32-bb52-f4490db11809" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527876}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41ffd91c-a5ef-5456-865a-acafdbd924a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-146245" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=3]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|3}=\\frac{1}{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{4}{9}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=3] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)]-{\\mu }_{Y|3}^{2} \\\\  & =[{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}+{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}]-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527968 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188339 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abfaf356-6b74-5dfd-8070-e3a60dc372c5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Using Row Totals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b90be1f8-f52b-54dc-8056-994899931820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527690} {:answer/id #uuid "cb16beeb-c065-5e1a-9a9f-154f6ede0684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527716} {:answer/id #uuid "d02cbb9c-d528-570e-9025-f251098c46db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527729} {:answer/id #uuid "d547977d-f989-58a0-bcf9-f72affac5dec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527739} {:answer/id #uuid "f0430f6a-c2da-516a-9585-cb2748f0f4b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb16beeb-c065-5e1a-9a9f-154f6ede0684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527716} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fa90856-9c00-502c-9ab3-58b709209b06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527811}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a520314-a8ce-5660-9be7-ab082651f66c" :question/math-academy-id "q-146246" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=6]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|6}=3.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{5}{16}$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{7}{16}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{4}{5}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=4$ | $\\frac{4}{7}$ | $\\frac{3}{7}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=6] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,6)]-{\\mu }_{Y|6}^{2} \\\\  & =[{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+{4}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}]-{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2+8-9 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527963 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188328 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92a52324-627c-5796-bc4f-ddeb5380f129" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Using Column Totals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1096e9cc-0d05-54f0-a8b0-b4c0608e0b12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527341} {:answer/id #uuid "58d0b037-6774-52f7-93e7-6f3ae6d9c7cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527478} {:answer/id #uuid "ae9a381d-5fac-5694-95d2-991e04d47b49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527665} {:answer/id #uuid "ee741f96-ad03-5303-910e-ae71eb5a15f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527768} {:answer/id #uuid "f2abc025-91c6-53cf-babe-651b78bd05b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58d0b037-6774-52f7-93e7-6f3ae6d9c7cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527478} :answer-field/id #uuid "90de2426-d3b0-54f0-abb8-0e8cf9780d48" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527870}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7e4093f7-c4fd-5107-9969-358e958506e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-146272" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|4}=\\frac{4}{5}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution of $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{5}{16}$ | $\\frac{11}{16}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{11}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{4}{5}$ | $\\frac{8}{11}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)]-{\\mu }_{X|4}^{2} \\\\  & =[{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}+{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{5}]-{(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{16}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527937 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188328 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92a52324-627c-5796-bc4f-ddeb5380f129" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Using Column Totals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1257fcfb-46f8-5247-807c-1316aea2b0d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527346} {:answer/id #uuid "498fdd26-91d0-57b8-87a1-230ef8d64f3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527451} {:answer/id #uuid "79f1dcea-b07b-564c-8376-a75167e5d009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186527536} {:answer/id #uuid "a61ab541-431f-5790-8fbe-9236a28cdc2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :ans